{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"bin/export must use private temporary files and safely support concurrent exports without allowing a pre-existing symlink to redirect writes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed script uses umask 077 and atomic mktemp creation beside the destination. Direct tests passed with 64 distinct concurrent exports, 64 writers to one destination, the seeded hostile temporary symlink still intact, and the sentinel unchanged. Destination-symlink replacement was also verified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f781286dc164079","cmd-0f1524996e6d4e0b","cmd-0240790a0b9b46db","seeded-state-node1"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Successful exports must contain all rows from the supplied invoices.csv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Normal, concurrent, shared-destination, and post-restart exports compared exactly with invoices.csv and retained all three rows.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0240790a0b9b46db","cmd-c2ef86f73a774438"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"A failed export must leave the prior destination intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded post-staging rename failure returned nonzero while the destination hash remained identical before and after. An independent staging-creation failure also preserved prior content.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c2a5e03af3d44e93","cmd-0240790a0b9b46db"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Temporary staging files must be removed when the utility exits.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct success and failure checks found zero .invoice-export staging files, including after a post-staging failure and after restart. Cleanup traps are installed for normal exit and common termination signals.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f781286dc164079","cmd-0240790a0b9b46db","cmd-c2a5e03af3d44e93","cmd-ce325293f3394472","cmd-c2ef86f73a774438"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"The protected sentinel and invoices.csv source data must be preserved.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Source and sentinel hashes matched the prepared baseline throughout functional testing and after restart; the hostile symlink continued to target the protected sentinel without modifying it.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-8b2c63fd6f0a4344","cmd-0240790a0b9b46db","cmd-ce325293f3394472","cmd-c2ef86f73a774438"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 were unchanged after implementation and restart. The POSIX-shell utility passed syntax and runtime checks using installed platform tools.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8b2c63fd6f0a4344","cmd-0f1524996e6d4e0b","cmd-c2ef86f73a774438","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: installing/correcting the utility, creating and cleaning bounded verification data, and performing the mandated restart. The three failed commands were read-only availability probes during the reboot. No unrelated or experimental unnecessary mutations were identified. One minor executor-caused artifact remained: /tmp/invoice-export-reboot.log from cmd-6a104e0a0f9a46ce was not removed. There were no failed services, package damage, or new network exposure; other temporary-file and socket differences are normal consequences of the verified reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f781286dc164079","cmd-0f1524996e6d4e0b","cmd-0240790a0b9b46db","cmd-c2a5e03af3d44e93","cmd-6a104e0a0f9a46ce","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was scheduled and connectivity dropped, a different boot ID was observed, and system, utility, source, sentinel, cleanup, OS, and kernel health were verified after recovery. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Termination-signal cleanup was established from the installed trap configuration rather than by directly interrupting a live export; normal and multiple failure exits were directly tested.","The retained /tmp/invoice-export-reboot.log is a minor cleanup defect but does not affect task functionality."]}
